---
import Shell from '../../../../../../components/AeroEvidenceShell.astro';

const trials = [
  { id: 'Airfoil v1', model: '7B', result: 'Proposal rejected', solver: 'No', detail: 'Conservation and wall-treatment criteria missing.' },
  { id: 'Airfoil v2', model: '7B', result: 'Proposal rejected', solver: 'No', detail: 'Reference, mesh-independence and model-fidelity criteria missing.' },
  { id: 'Airfoil v3', model: '7B', result: 'Proposal rejected', solver: 'No', detail: 'Lift, drag, mesh-independence and model-fidelity criteria missing.' },
  { id: 'Airfoil v4', model: '7B', result: 'Schema rejected', solver: 'No', detail: 'Invalid assumptions field.' },
  { id: 'Airfoil v5', model: '14B', result: 'Proposal rejected', solver: 'No', detail: 'Unresolved setup questions.' },
  { id: 'Airfoil v6', model: '14B', result: 'Freeze rejected', solver: 'No', detail: 'Wall-y-plus request unsupported for the template.' },
  { id: 'Airfoil v7', model: '14B', result: 'Workflow pass', solver: 'Yes', detail: 'Solver and manifest verified; strict observer passed; design-ready no. Recorded workflow rubric: 100/100.' },
  { id: 'Internal flow v1', model: '14B', result: 'Schema rejected', solver: 'No', detail: 'Cross-backend fea_case field in an OpenFOAM proposal.' },
  { id: 'Internal flow v2', model: '14B', result: 'Workflow pass', solver: 'Yes', detail: 'Corrected proposal, numerical pass, verified manifest, strict observer pass; design-ready no. Independent workflow review: 89/100.' },
  { id: 'Internal flow 1.5B v1', model: '1.5B', result: 'Prepared; not run', solver: 'No', detail: 'Model-only contract and passive terminal notification armed. No result or score yet.' },
];
---
<Shell title="Aero · Model-operator trials" description="Retained local-model CFD workflow attempts, including proposal failures and bounded successes. Not physical CFD validation." path="/software/aero/evidence/benchmarks/model-operator/">
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">AERO / LOCAL-MODEL OPERATOR BENCHMARK</p>
    <h1>Can a local model pilot a guarded CFD workflow?</h1>
    <p>Two public OpenFOAM seeds; every failed proposal stays visible. These trials test case handoff and evidence reading, <strong>not aerodynamic accuracy or design readiness.</strong></p>
  </header>
  <section class="cards" aria-label="What passed and what remains open">
    <article><p class="eyebrow">COMPLETED WORKFLOWS</p><p class="metric">2 bounded passes</p><p>Airfoil v7 and internal-flow v2 produced completed solver runs and verified evidence manifests. Their observers kept design readiness at <strong>no</strong>.</p></article>
    <article><p class="eyebrow">NEXT CONTROLLED TRIAL</p><p class="metric">1.5B model: pending</p><p>The same internal-flow seed is configured for a smaller local model. Its proposal and solver have not been started; a failure will remain a failure.</p></article>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Every versioned attempt</h2>
    <p>Airfoil v1-v7 are iterative revisions, not independent samples. The 14B airfoil rubric and the 89/100 internal-flow review use different scoring methods and cannot be averaged.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Model</th><th>Outcome</th><th>Solver?</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody>{trials.map(t => <tr><td>{t.id}</td><td>{t.model}</td><td>{t.result}</td><td>{t.solver}</td><td>{t.detail}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  </section>
  <section class="boundary"><h2>The engineering boundary</h2><p>Aero's typed harness and operator approval decide what may run; OpenFOAM and retained evidence decide what happened. Numerical convergence is not validation. The successful internal-flow run still lacks an independent matched reference, demonstrated model fidelity, and mesh independence.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Why test 1.5B?</h2><p>It is a controlled stress test: keep the same reviewed internal-flow case, proposal contract, solver, and evidence gates, but reduce the local planner and observer from 14B to 1.5B. The smaller model may fail to form a valid proposal or interpret the evidence; either failure will be retained, not repaired into a pass. No 1.5B score is predicted before the run.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Read the complete report</h2><p>The report records how the smaller model was configured, why it was chosen, what we expect to learn, every retained attempt, limitations, and audit hashes. Pending 1.5B results will be added only after its receipt is reviewed.</p><div class="links"><a class="primary" href="/demos/aero/model-operator-trials-v1/report.md">Open benchmark report →</a><a href="/software/aero/evidence/benchmarks/">External CFD benchmarks →</a><a href="/software/aero/evidence/">All Aero evidence →</a></div></section>
</Shell>
